    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d142-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d142-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, OSD Files: FRC 330–76–28, Office
                    Chrons, June–Aug 1969. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d142-f2" n="2" xml:id="d142-f2-content">
                <p>In this meeting, Laird stated that it was important to discontinue the use of the
                    term CBW term as such since it lumps together two separate programs, one for
                    chemical warfare and one for biological research.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
